# Line endings (issue #256): Dex verifies the exact bytes of tracked files
# against release hashes — the installed-files manifest is bound to the
# release catalog, and catalog items declare per-file hashes for their
# payloads. Git's own recommended core.autocrlf=true on Windows converts
# text files to CRLF on checkout, which broke every such check on every
# Windows install. Force LF on checkout everywhere so working-copy bytes
# always match the committed (and hashed) bytes.
* text=auto eol=lf
System/.installed-files.manifest text eol=lf

